📅 Day 55 – Servlet + JSP + JDBC Integration

Full Stack Web Development with Java Internship

Today’s session focused on integrating Servlet, JSP, and JDBC to understand how a complete web application workflow is built. The mentor explained how these components interact to process user requests and display dynamic data.

🔹 Topics Covered
1️⃣ Web Application Flow
User sends request from JSP page
Servlet receives and processes the request
JDBC is used to interact with the database
Response is forwarded to JSP for display
2️⃣ Role of Each Component
JSP → User interface (view layer)
Servlet → Handles logic and request processing (controller)
JDBC → Performs database operations (model/data layer)
3️⃣ Data Flow Process
User enters data in JSP form
Data is sent to Servlet
Servlet processes and stores data using JDBC
Data is retrieved from database
Result is displayed on JSP page
🔹 Practical Work

During the practice session, I:

Created JSP forms to collect user input
Developed servlets to process requests
Used JDBC to store and retrieve data
Forwarded results to JSP for display

This helped me understand the complete integration of frontend, backend, and database.